stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> Disabled

    Disabled --> Unplugged : Enable
    Unplugged --> Disabled : Disable
    Plugged --> Disabled : Disable
    Charging --> Disabled : Disable

    Plugged --> Unplugged : BspEvent(Disconnected)

    state Active <<choice>>
    Plugged --> Active
    Active --> Charging : see ISO / AC IEC diagrams

    Unplugged --> Plugged : A/B/C presence edge or present on entry
    Active --> ChargerFault : BspEvent(E/F)
    Unplugged --> ChargerFault : BspEvent(E/F), start pending
    ChargerFault --> Plugged : BspEvent(A) / duty in (4,97), fresh session
    ChargerFault --> Unplugged : BspEvent(Disconnected)
    ChargerFault --> Disabled : Disable

    note right of ChargerFault
        E/F in Plugged, SlacMatching, V2GNegotiating,
        BcbToggling, Charging, ChargingPwmPaused,
        Paused or Stopping, or in Unplugged with a start
        pending, is a charger fault: abort ISO, disable power,
        set CP B, reset SLAC, then report it on e2m/fault.
        Repeated E/F is ignored.
    end note

    Plugged --> Faulted : InternalFault
    Charging --> Faulted : InternalFault
    Faulted --> Unplugged : BspEvent(Disconnected)

    note right of Disabled
        Every non-Faulted active state accepts Disable
        and routes to Disabled (SlacMatching,
        V2GNegotiating, BcbToggling, Paused, Stopping,
        ChargingPwmPaused too, not just the arrows
        shown). Faulted ignores Disable.
    end note
